    "decoded_sample": "Vulkan compute dispatches require memory barriers because the driver and hardware may reorder memory accesses or execute them out of order to optimize performance, which can lead to data races if not explicitly synchronized. Without barriers, a shader might read stale data written by a previous dispatch or fail to see updates made by other threads within the same dispatch, violating the expected memory model. Barriers enforce a strict ordering of memory operations, ensuring that all writes are visible to subsequent reads and that synchronization points are respected across different compute workloads.\n\nThe user wants a three-sentence explanation of why Vulkan compute dispatches need memory barriers. Let me",
